      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patients' concerns about reporting pain and using analgesics have been cited as major contributors to the problem of inadequate pain management. The purpose of this paper is to describe a program of research in which we have focused on these patient concerns, or as we refer to them, \"patient-related barriers to pain management.\" We present a summary of descriptive studies on this topic, describe educational interventions that have been tested, and suggest future avenues of research and practice."},
